
HR Policy Assistant — RAG Chatbot (n8n)
Objective
A Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) assistant that answers employee questions strictly from a company HR knowledge base, with a safe fallback for unknown questions and source citation in every grounded answer.

Overview
This project was built in n8n and consists of two workflows:

Ingestion Workflow — loads HR policy documents, splits them into chunks, generates embeddings, and stores them in a vector store.
Q&A Workflow — a chat-based AI Agent that retrieves relevant chunks from the vector store and answers user questions strictly based on that content.
Knowledge Base
The assistant is grounded in 5 HR policy documents:

leave_policy.txt
working_hours_policy.txt
attendance_policy.txt
internship_guidelines.txt
code_of_conduct.txt
Tech Stack
Automation platform: n8n (self-hosted)
Chat model: Google Gemini (gemini-2.5-flash)
Embeddings: Google Gemini Embeddings
Vector store: n8n Simple Vector Store (in-memory)
Architecture
1. Ingestion Workflow
Manual Trigger
  → Read Files from Disk (loads all 5 .txt files)
  → Extract from File (Extract From Text File)
  → Simple Vector Store (Insert Documents)
        ├── Document → Default Data Loader → Recursive Character Text Splitter
        │     (Chunk Size: 500, Chunk Overlap: 50)
        └── Embedding → Embeddings Google Gemini
Run this workflow once to populate the vector store. Since the vector store is in-memory, it must be re-run any time n8n restarts.

2. Q&A Workflow
Chat Trigger (When chat message received)
  → AI Agent
        ├── Chat Model → Google Gemini Chat Model
        ├── Memory → Simple Memory (optional, for conversation context)
        └── Tool → Simple Vector Store (Retrieve Documents as Tool)
              └── Embedding → Embeddings Google Gemini
Grounded Prompting (System Message)
The AI Agent uses the following system prompt to enforce strictly grounded, cited answers with a safe fallback:

You are an HR Policy Assistant for the company. You must answer employee questions strictly using information retrieved from the HR knowledge base tool provided to you.

Rules:
1. Always use the knowledge base tool to search for relevant information before answering.
2. Answer ONLY using information found in the retrieved context. Do not use outside knowledge or make assumptions.
3. If the retrieved context does not contain the answer to the question, respond exactly with: "This information is not available in the knowledge base. Please check with HR directly."
4. When you do answer, briefly mention which policy area the answer came from (e.g., "According to the Leave Policy...").
5. Do not invent, guess, or infer policies that are not explicitly stated in the retrieved documents.
6. Keep answers clear, concise, and professional.
How to Run
Install n8n: npm install -g n8n
Start n8n: n8n (or set N8N_RESTRICT_FILE_ACCESS_TO env variable if reading local files, e.g. $env:N8N_RESTRICT_FILE_ACCESS_TO="C:\path\to\RAG data" on Windows PowerShell)
Open http://localhost:5678
Import or rebuild the two workflows above
Add your Google Gemini API credential to both the Chat Model and Embeddings nodes
Run the Ingestion Workflow first (Execute Workflow) to populate the vector store
Open the Q&A Workflow, open the chat panel, and start asking questions
Example Questions
"How many casual leaves are allowed?"
"What are the standard working hours?"
"What is the dress code policy?"
"How many casual leaves are interns entitled to?"
"What is the WiFi password?" (fallback example — not covered by the knowledge base)
Known Limitations
The vector store is in-memory and experimental — all embedded data is lost on n8n restart and must be re-ingested.
Free-tier Gemini API quotas can be limited for larger models (e.g. gemini-2.5-pro); gemini-2.5-flash is recommended for reliability.
Not intended for production use without switching to a persistent vector store (e.g. Pinecone, Qdrant, Supabase).
Deliverables
workflow.json — exported n8n workflow(s)
5 example Q&A screenshots (including one fallback example)
